  "timeMinutes": null,
  "type": "mc",
  "prompt": "The right-angled triangle $ABC$ has sides with lengths $a$ and $b$ as shown. The ratio of the area of the shaded square to the area of triangle $ABC$ is",
  "image": "qimages/samf/senior-2004-r1/q17.webp",
  "choices": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "$\\frac{ab}{a+b}$"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "$\\frac{ab}{(b-a)^2}$"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "$\\frac{2ab}{a^2+b^2}$"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "$\\frac{2ab}{(a+b)^2}$"
   },
   {
    "key": "E",
    "text": "$\\frac{ab}{(a+b)^2}$"
   }
  ],
  "answer": "D",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Similar triangles",
    "body": "Let the square have side $x$. The small white triangle at the top is similar to the whole triangle, so $\\frac{b-x}{x}=\\frac ba$, giving $x=\\frac{ab}{a+b}$. The ratio is $\\frac{x^2}{\\frac12ab}=\\frac{a^2b^2}{(a+b)^2}\\cdot\\frac{2}{ab}=\\frac{2ab}{(a+b)^2}$.\n\n**Answer: (D)**"
   }
  ],
