  "type": "mc",
  "prompt": "In the diagram, $MP$ is the perpendicular bisector of $BC$ and the length of $AB$ is 1. The length of $MP$ is",
  "image": "qimages/samf/senior-2004-r1/q19.webp",
  "choices": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "$\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{2a^2-1}}$"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "$a\\sqrt{4a^2-1}$"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "$\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{4a^2+1}}$"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "$\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{4a^2-1}}$"
   },
   {
    "key": "E",
    "text": "$\\frac12$"
   }
  ],
  "answer": "D",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Similar triangles",
    "body": "$BC=2a$ and $AC=\\sqrt{4a^2-1}$. Right triangles $CMP$ and $CAB$ share the angle at $C$, so $\\frac{MP}{MC}=\\frac{AB}{AC}$, giving $MP=\\frac{a\\cdot1}{\\sqrt{4a^2-1}}$.\n\n**Answer: (D)**"
   }
  ],
